{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-9x:000001:issue_created:sase-9x","timestamp":"2026-07-27T10:37:04Z","actor":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-9x","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-9x","title":"Make bead event-stream merges stable under rebase replay","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-07-27T10:37:04Z","created_by":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","updated_at":"2026-07-27T10:37:04Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"Concurrent bead writers in every plans-sidecar clone converge without human intervention: a multi-commit rebase replays to completion, derived bead files stay byte-stable across the Rust and Python writers, unpushed bead commits are never discarded, and recurring sync failure is surfaced as a health signal instead of surfacing as a hand-resolved merge conflict.","notes":"","design":"sase/repos/plans/202607/bead_merge_replay_stability.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","dependencies":[]}}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-9x:000002:issue_created:sase-9x.1","timestamp":"2026-07-27T10:37:08Z","actor":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-9x.1","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-9x.1","title":"Position-independent event identity and replay-stable stream merge","status":"open","issue_type":"phase","parent_id":"sase-9x","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-07-27T10:37:08Z","created_by":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","updated_at":"2026-07-27T10:37:08Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"merge: stop renumbering already-recorded bead events during stream merge, give newly created events collision-free identities, and replace the positional append-only check with an order-preserving containment check so a merge result stays a valid ancestor for the next replayed commit.","notes":"","design":"","model":"","size":"large","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","dependencies":[]}}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-9x:000003:issue_created:sase-9x.2","timestamp":"2026-07-27T10:37:11Z","actor":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-9x.2","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-9x.2","title":"Byte-identical JSONL encoding across both store writers","status":"open","issue_type":"phase","parent_id":"sase-9x","owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-07-27T10:37:11Z","created_by":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","updated_at":"2026-07-27T10:37:11Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"encoding: make the Python conflict resolver emit the same UTF-8 JSONL bytes as the Rust writer so resolution stops rewriting untouched streams with escaped-unicode churn that manufactures spurious merge rejections.","notes":"","design":"","model":"","size":"small","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","dependencies":[]}}}
